    en: "Mansourah Fortress is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Algeria. The ruins of Mansourah in Tlemcen testify to a formerly massive fortified city built by the Marinids during a siege. The imposing minaret is the most striking remnant. Built in the 14th century. Marinid ruins. 38-meter tall minaret. This landmark is part of the cultural heritage of Algeria, reflecting Berber, Arab and Mediterranean influences. Like many notable places in Algeria, it combines Berber heritage with Mediterranean and Saharan influences. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Algeria."
